      "side": 1,
      "message": "The access UIDs part of this change in itself LGTM.\n\nThe reshuffling of the code that happens when a network connects and sends its first updates looks like it could be an improvement, but I think it should be moved to its own CL so it can be carefully reviewed (remember that it\u0027s going to go out in a mainline release soon after being merged, and we\u0027ll want to make sure it doesn\u0027t negatively affect behaviour in the field. Not sure if the access UIDs part of the CL still depends on this reshuffling (IIRC it wasn\u0027t present a few patchsets ago).\n\nAlso I think it would be better for the code that implements the checks on the access UIDs to move to ConnectivityService or NetworkAgentInfo where it\u0027s called.",
      "revId": "16eb3b09ac4057abd4ed0a2435be6f83343f10f2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
