      "writtenOn": "2022-01-24T15:42:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I *think* this shuffling around of the code that \"intercepts\" NetworkAgent messages is an improvement, but it\u0027s difficult to tell within this this larger patch. It\u0027s also subtle and the kind of thing that could lead to hard-to-spot ordering bugs in the next mainline release. Do you think you could split it out to its own CL so it can be reviewed in isolation? That would also allow you to give that CL a detailed commit message explaining why it doesn\u0027t change any ordering (or that if it does, the changes don\u0027t matter).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6908,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6917,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "16eb3b09ac4057abd4ed0a2435be6f83343f10f2",
